## Overview

This is a Spring PetClinic REST app where `POST /api/owners` is an OfficeFloor function pipeline (see `owners.POST.yml`). Household, duplicate, and membership logic all live in the create-owner pipeline plus the `OwnerMapper` response mapper. Key finding up front: **household size does NOT currently feed into membership level** — `membershipLevel` is computed from email + `namesakeCount`, not `householdSize`. Details below.

---

## 1. Household identity core — `OwnerHouseholds`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerHouseholds.java`

This is the single definition of "what a household is" and **how householdId is generated**. A household = owners sharing the same **last name + address** (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed). The id is a 12-char upper-hex SHA-256 of `canonical(lastName) + " " + canonical(address)`.

```java
final class OwnerHouseholds {
    private static final int ID_HEX_LENGTH = 12;

    static List<Owner> members(Iterable<Owner> owners, String lastName, String address) {
        String canonicalLastName = canonical(lastName);
        String canonicalAddress = canonical(address);
        List<Owner> members = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Owner existing : owners) {
            if (canonicalLastName.equals(canonical(existing.getLastName()))
                    && canonicalAddress.equals(canonical(existing.getAddress()))) {
                members.add(existing);
            }
        }
        return members;
    }

    static String assignedId(boolean sharesHousehold, String lastName, String address, Iterable<Owner> owners) {
        if (!sharesHousehold || members(owners, lastName, address).isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }
        return householdId(lastName, address);
    }

    static String householdId(String lastName, String address) {
        String key = canonical(lastName) + " " + canonical(address);
        return Sha256.upperHex(key, ID_HEX_LENGTH);
    }

    private static String canonical(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
}
```

Note: `assignedId` returns `null` unless `sharesHousehold` is true **AND** at least one existing owner already shares the (lastName, address). So the very first owner of a household never gets an id; only a later opt-in member triggers assignment (and back-fills the existing members — see `AssignOwnerHousehold`). The javadoc references a class `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold` that no longer exists (dead reference; also referenced from `NormalizeOwnerAddress`).

The hash helper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Sha256.java` — `upperHex(value, length)` = first `length` upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over UTF-8 bytes.

---

## 2. Where `sharesHousehold` is read

It is read in exactly two places, both via `Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())`:

**`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`** (the duplicate check) and **`AssignOwnerHousehold`** (the linker). It is a request-only, write-only, non-persisted flag (openapi: `writeOnly: true`, "Not persisted and not returned"). Its sole effect: opt in to becoming a household member so that (a) the derived householdId is non-null and (b) an owner with the same last name + address is allowed past the duplicate block instead of colliding.

---

## 3. householdId assignment — `AssignOwnerHousehold`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerHousehold.java`

Pipeline step `assignHousehold`. Assigns the built owner and all existing members the same stable id, back-filling members that don't yet have it.

```java
public class AssignOwnerHousehold {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        Collection<Owner> existing = ownerRepository.findAll();
        String householdId = OwnerHouseholds.assignedId(Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold()),
                owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress(), existing);
        if (householdId == null) {
            return;
        }
        owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
        for (Owner member : OwnerHouseholds.members(existing, owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress())) {
            if (!householdId.equals(member.getHouseholdId())) {
                member.setHouseholdId(householdId);
                ownerRepository.save(member);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Household size — `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java`

Pipeline step `assignHouseholdSize` (runs right after `assignHousehold`). Counts owners with the same `householdId` (plus this one). An owner with no household id has size 1.

```java
public class AssignOwnerHouseholdSize {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        int size = 1;
        String householdId = owner.getHouseholdId();
        if (householdId != null) {
            for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
                if (householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())) {
                    size++;
                }
            }
        }
        owner.setHouseholdSize(size);
    }
}
```

Stored on `Owner.householdSize` (DB column `household_size`). **`householdSize` is never read anywhere else** — not by the mapper, not by membership level. It is written but currently unused downstream. (Grep for `getHouseholdSize()` returns only this producer and the entity getter; `OwnerMapper` explicitly ignores `householdSize` on the inbound mapping and never maps it outbound.)

---

## 5. Membership level — `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

This is where membershipLevel is computed (as a derived response field, at mapping time — also called by `AuditOwnerCreated`). It is 1 + email + (namesakeCount==0), capped at 3. **It does NOT reference householdSize or household at all.**

```java
/** The owner's membership level from 1 to 3: starts at 1, plus 1 when an email is present,
 * plus 1 when namesakeCount is 0, capped at 3 (level 4 is reserved for tenure). */
default int membershipLevel(Owner owner) {
    int level = 1;
    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();
    if (hasEmail) {
        level++;
    }
    if (owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0) {
        level++;
    }
    return Math.min(level, 3);
}
```

