## 1. Household identity core — `OwnerHouseholds`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerHouseholds.java`

This is the single definition of "what a household is" and **how householdId is generated**. A household = owners sharing the same **last name + address** (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed). The id is a 12-char upper-hex SHA-256 of `canonical(lastName) + " " + canonical(address)`.

```java
final class OwnerHouseholds {
    private static final int ID_HEX_LENGTH = 12;

    static List<Owner> members(Iterable<Owner> owners, String lastName, String address) {
        String canonicalLastName = canonical(lastName);
        String canonicalAddress = canonical(address);
        List<Owner> members = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Owner existing : owners) {
            if (canonicalLastName.equals(canonical(existing.getLastName()))
                    && canonicalAddress.equals(canonical(existing.getAddress()))) {
                members.add(existing);
            }
        }
        return members;
    }

    static String assignedId(boolean sharesHousehold, String lastName, String address, Iterable<Owner> owners) {
        if (!sharesHousehold || members(owners, lastName, address).isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }
        return householdId(lastName, address);
    }

    static String householdId(String lastName, String address) {
        String key = canonical(lastName) + " " + canonical(address);
        return Sha256.upperHex(key, ID_HEX_LENGTH);
    }

    private static String canonical(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
}
```

Note: `assignedId` returns `null` unless `sharesHousehold` is true **AND** at least one existing owner already shares the (lastName, address). So the very first owner of a household never gets an id; only a later opt-in member triggers assignment (and back-fills the existing members — see `AssignOwnerHousehold`). The javadoc references a class `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold` that no longer exists (dead reference; also referenced from `NormalizeOwnerAddress`).

The hash helper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Sha256.java` — `upperHex(value, length)` = first `length` upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over UTF-8 bytes.

