## 6. Duplicate detection — how it keys off household

There are TWO distinct duplicate mechanisms:

### (a) Hard duplicate → 409: `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java` (pipeline step `rejectDuplicateIdentity`).

Keys off the **identity key** `telephone | email | householdId`. This is where household enters duplicate detection: the would-be householdId (from `OwnerHouseholds.assignedId`, same logic `AssignOwnerHousehold` will store) is part of the key.

```java
public class RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateOwnerException {
        Collection<Owner> existing = ownerRepository.findAll();
        String householdId = OwnerHouseholds.assignedId(Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold()),
                request.getLastName(), request.getAddress(), existing);
        String identityKey = OwnerIdentity.key(request.getTelephone(), request.getEmail(), householdId);
        for (Owner owner : existing) {
            if (identityKey.equals(OwnerIdentity.of(owner))) {
                throw new DuplicateOwnerException(identityKey);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The key definition — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/OwnerIdentity.java`:

```java
public static String key(String telephone, String email, String householdId) {
    return part(telephone) + '|' + part(email) + '|' + part(householdId);
}
public static String of(Owner owner) {
    return key(owner.getTelephone(), owner.getEmail(), owner.getHouseholdId());
}
private static String part(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value;
}
```

The exception + handler:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateOwnerException.java` — `extends Exception`, message `"An owner with identity key " + identityKey + " already exists"`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateOwnerExceptionHandler.java` — responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`.
- Wired by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateOwnerException.yml`.

### (b) Soft/possible duplicate (non-blocking): `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java` (pipeline step `assignPossibleDuplicate`).

This one does **NOT** key off household — it keys off **lastName + postcode + a *different* telephone**. Sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the lowest-id match. Never rejects.

```java
public class AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String lastName = canonical(owner.getLastName());
        String postcode = trimmed(owner.getPostcode());
        String telephone = trimmed(owner.getTelephone());
        if (postcode == null) {
            return; // no postcode to share, so no soft match
        }
        Owner match = null;
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (lastName.equals(canonical(existing.getLastName()))
                    && postcode.equals(trimmed(existing.getPostcode()))
                    && !Objects.equals(telephone, trimmed(existing.getTelephone()))
                    && (match == null || existing.getId() < match.getId())) {
                match = existing;
            }
        }
        if (match != null) {
            owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(match.getId());
        }
    }
    private static String canonical(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
    private static String trimmed(String value) {
        if (value == null) return null;
        String trimmed = value.trim();
        return trimmed.isEmpty() ? null : trimmed;
    }
}
```

